					<h1 class="title" title="Vaishnodevi Tourism">Vaishnodevi Tour</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">
 <p>
       
        Vaishno Devi Almost a million years old holy shrine of Shri Mata Vaishno Devi is 
        most popular and one of the holiest pilgrimage sites in India. The people all 
        over the world believe that no one returns empty handed once they have come in 
        the shadow of mother goddess. So the popular quote <b>'Moonh Maangi Muradein Poori 
        Karne Wali Mata' </b>is always been used for her.
    </p>
    <p>
       
        Vaishno Devi Ma is believed to 
        righteously grant everything that a person wishes for in life to those who visit 
        Her Holy Shrine with full devotion, faith and pure heart. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        It is believed that 
        Mata Vaishno Devi had spent some time to observe spiritual corrections and 
        repentances at the Holy Shrine. The holy cave is treated sanctified because it 
        is said that this is the place where Mata merged her Human form with the astral 
        form of the three Supreme Energies. 
    </p>
<br/>
 <object classid="clsid:D27CDB6E-AE6D-11cf-96B8-444553540000" codebase="https://download.macromedia.com/pub/shockwave/cabs/flash/swflash.cab#version=9,0,28,0"

width="490" height="350">

<param name="movie" value="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Vaishnodevi/Vaishno Devi.swf" />

<param name="quality" value="high" />

<embed  src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/indiacitytrip.com/code/images/Vaishnodevi/Vaishno Devi.swf"  quality="high" pluginspage="https://www.adobe.com/shockwave/download/download.cgi?P1_Prod_Version=ShockwaveFlash" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="490" height="350"></embed>
<br/>
    <p>
       
        The 5200 ft high Holy Cave situated in three 
        peaked mountain Trikoot attracts lakhs of devotees not only from India but also 
        from abroad every year. Shri Mata Vaishno Devi Shrine Board formed in 1986 is 
        committed for proper management of the pilgrim site and Yatra. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        The Yatris have 
        to cover the trek of around 12 km from Katra. The narrow path gradually 
        proceeding to the holy shrine is covered at some places; many tea and snack 
        stalls are located alongside. At the end of this intricate path yatries 
        (devotees) are enthralled with the Darshans of the Mother Goddess in the Holy 
        Cave. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        The Cave does not have statues or idols or pictures instead the Darshan is 
        in the shape of three natural rock formations called the Pindies. You can visit 
        the court of Mata Vaishno Devi round the clock throughout the year. 
    </p>
    <h3>
       
        The 
        Offerings 
    </h3>
    <p>
       
        Traditional offerings are red Chunri, Saries, Cholas, Silver or Gold 
        ornaments, Dry Fruits, Flowers etc. but no sweets; Coconuts etc. are allowed 
        inside the Holy Cave. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        The donations are also accepted in the form of 
        cash/cheques/drafts. They are either put into the sealed donation boxes kept at 
        various places or at computerized donation counters. Similarly ornaments, 
        Saries, Cholas and Chunris are deposited in the jewelry boxes kept all around. 
        </p>
    <p>
       
        You need not carry Prashad/Bhaints from Katra, the Bhaint Shops of Shrine Board 
        there sell these at a fair price. All the donations to Shri Mata Vaishno Devi 
        Shrine Board enjoy tax benefits under section 80-G of the Income Tax Act. Tips 
        </p>
    <p>
       
        1. Obtain a Yatra slip for free from Yatra Registration Counter, near Katra bus 
        stand. This slip is checked at Banganga check post, without obtaining the Yatra 
        slip you cannot move forward. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        2. Rented accommodation at Katra, Adkuwari, 
        Sanjichhat or Bhawan, can be booked from the Enquiry and Reservation Counter at 
        Niharika Complex near Katra Bus Stand. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        3. Ensure that the Porters, Ponies and 
        Palanquins carry a valid registration card before hiring them also pay only 
        according to the pre-approved rate card.
    </p>
    <p>
       
        4. Carry bare minimum things with you. 
        </p>
    <p>
       
        5. Go to Yatra slip check post to get group number for getting into the queue 
        for Darshans. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        6. Before proceeding for the Darshans take a bath and wear clean 
        clothes. 
    </p>
    <p>
       
        7. Darshans at Bhairon temple are done after Darshans at the Holy Cave.
    </p>
    
